2.2.6
Tag Manager: click a tag to rename it across the library, or clear the name to delete it (#82)
Multi-Edit Edit Tags opens Tag Manager
Preview tiles show filenames without hovering (#81)
Click an expanded folder or ZIP group to collapse it; click empty grid space to deselect
Local OpenAI-compatible AI tagging servers no longer require an API key
Tag Manager Full Screen resizes the dialog and keeps existing tags visible (#80)
Library grid no longer stays empty on launch until you switch views

2.2.5
List view columns: show/hide, resize, and drag-to-reorder. Layout is saved.
Zip/group list rows use the same columns with aggregated metadata.
Printed column renamed to Print Status; sort headers show an arrow only.
MCP: tags, filaments, print events, metadata, thumbnails, and duplicates tools.
AI Tagging includes Claude (default claude-haiku-4-5).

2.2.4
HTTPS / SSL settings in Settings for server, Docker, and the desktop Browser Extension / MCP listener. Custom PEM, Let's Encrypt (HTTP-01), or self-signed.
Server/Docker HTTPS listen port (default 5000). Map the same port on the host.
PWA / mobile UI for server and Docker.
Browser Extension inbox: queue model pages/downloads without the app running, then import from the inbox folder.
AI Tagging now includes Claude as a provider (default model claude-haiku-4-5).

2.2.3
Print lifecycle and history: Unprinted / Want / Queued / Printing / Printed / Failed plus a dated print log (quantity, notes, filaments). Click a card badge to log a print; Shift-click changes status only. Filter Ever/Never printed; sort by last printed or print count.
Folder-tree library explorer: Folders filter with a popover tree of scanned directories, plus an optional Folders rail next to the grid. Click a folder to set the Directory chip.
Sidebar layout: search and sort stay pinned; the long filter stack auto-collapses when model details open. Sidebar and Folders panels are drag-resizable.
De-Dup can run on the current library view (designer, tags, query builder, and other filters) instead of always scanning the entire collection (#61).
Filament catalog with optional pull-only Spoolman sync; assign filaments to models and filter the library by them.
MCP Server (experimental): Tools → MCP Server enables a localhost /mcp endpoint for AI agents (always on in Docker/server). Tools include search_models, get_model, update_model, get_folder_tree, set_thumbnail, and more. Any client that can reach the endpoint can read/change library data — trusted networks only.
Nested .3mf models inside ZIP archives no longer fail hash generation. Docker/server Dedup hash timeout and Windows path-mount fixes remain.

2.2.0
Folder and ZIP bundle grouping — models that share a parent folder or ZIP archive appear as a single card with a details panel
Bundle 3D preview — open every STL/3MF part in a folder or ZIP in one grid layout with per-part colors
Send to Slicer from preview — send the current model or entire bundle to your configured slicer (new instance on macOS)
Query Builder, new Preview view, and customizable list columns
New models tagged "New" until edited, parent-model grouping, LYS/LTY file support, and library disk-usage stats
Docker/server NVIDIA GPU support, in-container thumbnail generation, and thumbnail progress UI
Bug fixes and performance optimization

2.1.21
Replaced Google Analytics (GA4) with GoatCounter for usage reporting. Still gated by Enable Usage Reporting in About.
First launch after install could leave Electron processes running with no visible window (kill in Task Manager, then relaunch worked). Main window now force-shows after a short timeout, second-instance focuses call show(), Chart.js/Fuse.js are vendored locally instead of blocking on a CDN, and UI load has a timeout with file:// fallback.

2.1.20
Stats panel shows total library disk usage and per-type byte sizes (3MF / STL / Other) alongside counts.
Grid multi-thumbnail carousel upgrades from list metadata (hasMultipleThumbnails) without loading full thumbnail blobs up front; default-thumbnail changes broadcast live so carousels stay in sync.
Bundle/archive details modal lists models instead of a contents table, with simpler layout and actions.

2.1.19
Directory labels in Detailed/List/details now show the full parent path (including drive letter) instead of only the leaf folder name, so thumbdrive/USB scans are not confused with similarly named folders on other drives. Files in the root of a drive show as E:\ (not a bare E:). Zip entries include the zip's on-disk location.
Grid thumbnail hydrate no longer logs Failed to generate thumbnail / Render task pruned when virtual-grid rebuilds or scroll drops off-screen queue jobs (expected). Also prevents a prune from clearing the pending slot while the same file is still mid-render, which could start duplicate concurrent loads.
On-screen models without thumbnails are re-queued after scroll prune / queue soft-cap. Virtual-grid was keeping recycled DOM cells and never calling createModelItem again, so visible placeholders could stay stuck on 3d.png even though priority favors the viewport.
ZIP/folder group cards and Generate Missing Thumbnails no longer stay stuck on 3d.png: detached renderModelToPNG callers now pass retainDetached so the post-load scroll-prune check does not abort after a successful load (regression from 2.1.17/2.1.18).

2.1.18
Desktop Scan Directory no longer hangs at 0/N after 2.1.17 scroll-queue prune (retainDetached for scan/batch thumbs)
Docker NVIDIA: stop forceContextLoss on thumbnail recycle (Skia OOM / CreateSharedImage log storms); soft-dispose + disable GPU compositing; cap NVIDIA WebGL concurrency to 1

